  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Preheat oven to 240°C/220°C fan-forced. Cut potato into bite-sized chunks. Place on a lined oven tray.\n• Sprinkle over garlic and herb seasoning. Drizzle with olive oil, season with salt and toss to coat. Roast until tender, 20-25 minutes.\n• Roughly chop tomato and cucumber. Cut or tear each spinach falafel into quarters (don't worry if they crumble!).",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/638ee51058e51c3eca0c70d8/step-aeeb054f.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• With 10 minutes cook time remaining on the potato, heat a large frying pan over medium-high heat and add olive oil (1/4 cup for 2 people / 1/2 cup for 4 people).\n• When oil is hot, add falafels and cook, tossing, until deep golden brown, 4-6 minutes. Transfer to a paper towel-lined plate.\n• Meanwhile, in a medium bowl, combine a drizzle of vinegar and olive oil. Season with salt and pepper. Add tomato, cucumber and mixed salad leaves. Toss to coat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/638ee51058e51c3eca0c70d8/step-3d65ff29.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Wipe out and return frying pan to medium heat. Add red pesto (see ingredients), light cooking cream and a pinch of pepper. Cook, stirring, until slightly thickened, 2-3 minutes. TIP: Add a splash more water if the sauce looks too thick.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/638ee51058e51c3eca0c70d8/step-8a8d9c65.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Divide spinach falafels, potato chunks and garden salad between plates.\n• Sprinkle flaked almonds over salad. Spoon creamy Italian sauce over falafels to serve. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/638ee51058e51c3eca0c70d8/step-94cec477.jpg"
    }
  ]
}
